This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. Its
items are Dr Henry J Grech-Cini's own house guidance for writing prose that does not
read as machine generated, expressed as a grounded IDD graph so consuming projects can
compose it with throughline-compose.

The catalogue of "tells" the rules invert is observed from Wikipedia's advice page
"Signs of AI writing" (WikiProject AI Cleanup), available under CC BY-SA. That page is
cited as the source of the observations only; none of its text is reproduced here. The
rule wording is original.
